msgid ""
"**With a mouse**: *right-click* on a window title, then click "
"on :guilabel:`Fullscreen`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:8
#: 202376efba29448caea21490d5e6145c
msgid ""
"**With a keyboard**: press :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`Space` and "
"select :guilabel:`Fullscreen` (or type :kbd:`F`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:9
#: 2055a117d984431ead0e519963bf66c4
msgid "**With a keyboard shortcut**: press :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`F11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:11
#: 71629d4164d14ffb982c9e0f6b54eb13
msgid ""
"This page discusses the security implications of fullscreen mode and "
"alternate solutions to allow fullscreen mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:14
#: c33c3763168b4f278ca3f1e5d754800e
msgid "What is fullscreen mode?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:16
#: 4eaee25ff2b1475789c665911d602293
msgid ""
"Normally, the Qubes GUI virtualization daemon restricts any qube from "
"”owning” the full screen, ensuring that there are always clearly marked "
"decorations drawn by the trusted Window Manager around each of the qubes' "
"windows. This allows the user to easily realize to which domain a specific "
"window belongs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:21
#: a87a26d4d01b4d2b87bda84b3e00c499
msgid "Trying to enter fullscreen mode from a qube fails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:23
#: 80962d9f67894247b72ed02e2677392f
msgid ""
"While browsing the page :doc:`/introduction/video-tours` in a disposable "
"qube (*disp5596*), the user tries to enter fullscreen mode from the qube "
"itself. Even if fullscreen mode is selected, the top bar of dom0 is still "
"present. The window is decorated in red, providing the name of the qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:26
#: cd58afe368224bc7badb55f746f0ceee
msgid "Why is fullscreen mode potentially dangerous?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:28
#: 5f5b434df250431b88d50ca0137bd570
msgid ""
"If one allowed a qube to “own” the full screen, e.g. to show a movie on a "
"full screen, it might not be possible for the user to know if the "
"application or the qube really “released” the full screen, or if it has "
"started emulating the whole desktop and is pretending to be the trusted "
"Window Manager, drawing shapes on the screen that look like other windows, "
"belonging to other domains (e.g. to trick the user into entering a secret "
"passphrase into a window that looks like belonging to some trusted domain)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:30
#: db0e8b6e9788432a8c9894cb23e257c2
msgid ""
"That's why fullscreen mode is not allowed by default, when requested from a "
"qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:35
#: c636d365c51e41868fedef0c4c656ec1
msgid "Secure use of fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:37
#: d223485091434322badc332420654ef0
msgid ""
"However, it is possible to deal with fullscreen mode in a secure way "
"assuming there are mechanisms that can be used at any time to switch between "
"windows or show the full desktop and that cannot be intercepted by the qube. "
"The simplest example is the use of :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`Tab` for switching "
"between windows, which is a shortcut handled by dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:39
#: 622e047769014f97a6630c15ff07c86d
msgid ""
"Other examples of such mechanisms are the KDE “Present Windows” and “Desktop "
"Grid” effects, which are similar to Mac’s “Expose” effect, and which can be "
"used to immediately detect potential “GUI forgery”, as they cannot be "
"intercepted by any of the qube (as the GUID never passes down the key "
"combinations that got consumed by the KDE Window Manager), and so the qube "
"cannot emulate those. Those effects are enabled by default in KDE once "
"Compositing gets enabled in KDE (:menuselection:`System Settings --> Desktop "
"--> Enable Desktop Effects`), which is recommended anyway. By default, they "
"are triggered by the :kbd:`Ctrl` + :kbd:`F8` and :kbd:`Ctrl` + :kbd:`F9` key "
"combinations, but can also be reassigned to other shortcuts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:42
#: 2a7f04e5a9f341ea8c4ee3417a5b9b15
msgid "Safely enabling fullscreen mode for a selected window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:44
#: fcba44fba1774770ab626b5f97bc8bec
msgid ""
"You can always put a window into fullscreen mode in Xfce4 using the trusted "
"window manager by right-clicking on a window’s title bar and "
"selecting :guilabel:`Fullscreen` or pressing :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`F11`. This "
"functionality should still be considered safe, since a qube window still "
"can’t voluntarily enter fullscreen mode. The user must select this option "
"from the trusted window manager in dom0. To exit fullscreen mode from here, "
"press :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`Space` to bring up the title bar menu again, then "
"select :guilabel:`Leave Fullscreen` or simply press :kbd:`Alt` + :kbd:`F11`. "
"For :term:`HVM`, you should set the screen resolution in the qube to that of "
"the host, (or larger), *before* setting fullscreen mode in Xfce4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:50
#: 9fa67bec926b422d9664a0952e5a4dfa
msgid "Enabling fullscreen mode from a selected qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:52
#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:78
#: 7fa09d5b25f8448cb72b973d81fe1343 29f8394cfc8146d5a91eefdcdb8d5ac8
msgid "Be sure to read :ref:`secure-use-of-fullscreen-mode` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:54
#: 86300d74b27d43b48b478725dfbd469a
msgid ""
"As an alternative to the Xfce4 method, you can enable fullscreen mode for "
"selected qubes by using a :doc:`gui-* <core-admin-client:manpages/qvm-"
"features>` feature called ``gui-allow-fullscreen``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-enter-fullscreen-mode.rst:56
#: bb3d9d11ac9745188d769372309ea657
msgid ""
